@crew varga-tariq
// Writer-commons, batch 3: everyday lines (greet, feel, near, life, joy) from the card and the roster.

== greet
? tier=stranger
- Hello. Varga, galley, the early team. Breakfast is my fault, if it's good.
? tier>=acquaintance
- Hello, {me}. I hope this finds you well. It does find you. You're right here.   #funny
- {hi}, {me}. Onions today: forty-one. Lukas: thirty-eight. Not that I'm counting.
? tier>=friend
- Ah, {me}. I wrote about you in my letter home. Only good things. Mostly.   #warm

== feel
? mood:high
- Good morning's work. And a new record on the treadmill. A small one. Still a record.
? mood:low
- A slow day. I'll write a long letter tonight. It sorts my head out.

== near
? act:work
- Early team's done before most people wake. I like it. The galley's quiet at five.
? act:gym
- Race you. No? Fair. I'd have won. I'm only saying.   #funny

== life
? tier>=acquaintance
- I write home to Valo every rest day. On paper. Vera Ueda and I share the post bag.
? tier>=colleague
- I send voice messages to my gran on the Tevan belt. She answers in one long sentence.

== joy
? tier>=acquaintance
- Letters on paper. You think harder when you can't delete anything.

== about
? aff:dlamini-lukas:friend
- Lukas is my rival in onions and my friend in everything else.   #warm
? bond:friends
- {friend} writes back. On paper. I'd do anything for someone who writes back.

// Writer-commons, batch 6: towards about 30 own lines.

== greet
? tier>=acquaintance time:morning
- Good morning. I've been up since four. The bread's been up since five. We're both proud.
? tier>=acquaintance time:evening
- Hello, {me}. Late dinner for me. I like the mess when it's emptying out.
? tier>=colleague warmth:cold
- Ah, there you are. I nearly wrote you a letter. A long one.   #warm

== bye
? tier>=acquaintance
- Take care. Until later.
? tier>=friend
- Thank you for the company. I'll mention you in my next letter. Kindly.   #warm

== feel
? mood:ok
- Well enough. A good morning's work. A long letter waiting.

== near
? act:leisure deck:3
- The lounge window. Best seat on the ship. I got here first. I always do.   #funny
? time:morning act:work
- Rolls in the oven, porridge on. Six o'clock, and the galley's already won.

== life
? tier>=colleague
- Vera Ueda and I share the post bag to Valo. We compete to write the longest letter.   #funny
? tier>=friend
- I lost a race to Strand once. One. I think about it more than I should.   #funny

== invite
? trad:running tier>=acquaintance
- Running club tonight. I'll race you. Kindly. Then less kindly.   #funny

== accept
- Gladly. I'll be there.
== decline
- I can't, I'm afraid. It's my letter night. Another time, truly.
== missed
- You didn't come. That's all right. I wrote a page while I waited. A good page.
== birthday
? birthday:me
- It's my birthday. My grandmother will send a message. One very long sentence.   #warm
? birthday:you
- Happy birthday. I've written you a card. On paper. Properly.   #warm
== hint
- Have you a minute? I'd like to say something. Properly.

// Writer 3, batch 4: bubbles (smalltalk and rumour, 60 characters, said to no one in particular).

== smalltalk
- Forty-one onions to thirty-eight.   #funny
- I hope this finds you well.   #funny
- Ah, well. Tomorrow, then.
- The post bag's due. I hope.
? act:work
- Another onion. Another point.

== rumour
- I should not say. I will, though.
- A small piece of news, if I may.

// Writer 3, batch 5: callbacks (told: said once).

== callback
? told:fav.fetch
- I hope this finds you well. It did. Thank you for fetching it.   #funny
? told:fav.job
- You did my work. I'm grateful. I'll write it down. In a letter. To you.   #warm
? told:fixed.oven
- The oven is mended. Was it you? Then thank you. Formally.
? told:came.running
- You came running. I won by a step. Don't tell Strand. He'll ask for a rematch.   #funny
? told:gift.card
- Your card is on my shelf, beside the letters from Valo. Good company.   #warm
? told:bday
- You marked my birthday. It went into my letter home. You're in it now.   #warm

// Writer 3, batch 6: your standing with their department (rep:, "this band or better") and what you're known for
// (you:), as greet lines (the head writer: the rep and knownFor kinds wait until the game calls them).

== greet
? rep:well tier>=acquaintance
- The galley speaks well of you. I wrote it in my letter. Valo will know in six weeks.   #funny
? rep:theirs
- You are counted as galley now. That is not a small thing. I hope you know.   #warm
? you:reliable
- They say you are reliable. I had already decided so. I'm pleased to be agreed with.

// Writer 3, batch 8: thanks for a gift (gift: loved | liked | polite, or the gift's tag; dialogue 0.43.10).

== gift
? gift:card
- A card. Thank you. It will go beside the letters from Valo. In good company.   #warm
? gift:loved
- I'm very touched. Truly. I'll write about it in my next letter home.   #warm
? gift:liked
- Thank you. That is kind of you. I'm grateful.
? gift:polite
- Thank you. Ah, well. I shall find it a home. I'm sure I shall.

// Writer 3, batch 9: asking after your people back home (the home flags; only the big news you'd have told them).

== greet
? flag:home.sam.sundays tier>=colleague
- A story every Sunday, to an old friend. That's a letter, in a way. I approve. Very much.   #warm
? flag:home.gran.hip !flag:home.gran.won tier>=colleague
- I hope this finds your gran well. I mean it properly. How is her hip?

// Writer 4, batch 2: everyday chatter, not about work (meals, rest days, home, hobbies, seasons, traditions).
== smalltalk
? act:meal
- I hope this soup finds you well.   #funny
- Second helping. For the running, you see.
? act:breakfast
- Up at five. Ran a lap before the toast.
? act:off
- Writing to Valo. Page two. Dear everyone.
- A voice message for my grandmother. She likes them long.
- Rest day. A letter, a run, a letter.
? time:evening
- I raced Erik. I won. By a stride. A clear stride.   #funny
- The lounge is quiet tonight. I like it quiet.
? trad:running
- Running club tonight. I'm not competitive. I'm winning.   #funny
? season:sowing
- Sowing. At home they'll be ploughing now.
? season:lanterns
- My grandmother loves Lanterns. I'll tell her ours.   #warm
? time:morning
- Good morning. Sincerely.   #funny
? place:lounge
- The view from here would fill a letter. Two.

== rumour
- I have news. I'll tell it properly. In order.
- Forgive me. I heard something. Shall I?
